proof.text:
Let $u:K'\to K$ and $v:L\to L'$ be morphisms of Weil pairs. Their commuting equations from [def-wf-weil-category] give
$$\varphi_K^{-1}u=P(u)\varphi_{K'}^{-1},\qquad v\varphi_L=\varphi_{L'}P(v).$$
The comparison of [def-wf-internal-hom] is natural: on the displayed Hom complexes it sends a local map to its transport, so precomposition by $u$ and postcomposition by $v$ are sent to precomposition by $P(u)$ and postcomposition by $P(v)$. This equality descends to derived morphisms and is bilinear for the localized fraction rule. In symbols,
$$H(Pu,Pv)\alpha_{K,L}=\alpha_{K',L'}P(H(u,v)).$$
Using the two preceding commuting equations and contravariance in the first slot, the bifunctor laws now give
$$H(u,v)\beta_{K,L}
=H(\varphi_K^{-1}u,v\varphi_L)\alpha_{K,L}
=H(\varphi_{K'}^{-1},\varphi_{L'})H(Pu,Pv)\alpha_{K,L}
=\beta_{K',L'}P(H(u,v)).$$
This is exactly the morphism equation for the output Weil pairs.
